---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import LinkCard from '../../components/LinkCard.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const tools = [
  {
    title: 'Parlay Calculator',
    href: '/tools/parlay-calculator',
    description: 'Calculate potential parlay payouts and understand the true cost of combining bets.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Odds Converter',
    href: '/tools/odds-converter',
    description: 'Convert between American, decimal, and fractional odds formats.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Bankroll Calculator',
    href: '/tools/bankroll-calculator',
    description: 'Determine appropriate bet sizing based on your bankroll and risk tolerance.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Betting Calculators & Tools"
  description="Sports betting calculators and tools to support better decision-making. Parlay calculator, odds converter, and bankroll management tools."
>
  <Hero
    title="Betting Calculators & Tools"
    subtitle="Practical Tools to Support Better Betting Decisions"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            Betting tools help you make calculations quickly and accurately, but they don't replace judgment. A parlay calculator tells you potential payouts—it doesn't tell you whether the parlay is a good bet. Use these tools to support your process, not as a substitute for analysis. The best tool is a disciplined approach to betting; calculators just handle the math.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Why Use Betting Tools?" id="why-tools">
        <p>
          Betting involves math. Converting odds, calculating implied probability, determining appropriate bet sizes, and projecting parlay payouts all require arithmetic that's easy to get wrong under time pressure or emotional stress.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tools remove calculation errors from the equation, letting you focus on the harder questions: Is this bet worth making? Does my analysis suggest value here? Am I betting the right amount?
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What Can Tools Do?" id="what-can-do">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Save time:</strong> Instant calculations instead of manual math</li>
          <li><strong>Prevent errors:</strong> Eliminate arithmetic mistakes that cost money</li>
          <li><strong>Enable comparison:</strong> Quickly compare odds across different formats</li>
          <li><strong>Enforce discipline:</strong> Bankroll calculators help maintain consistent bet sizing</li>
          <li><strong>Reveal hidden costs:</strong> Parlay calculators show the compounding effect of the vig</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What Can Tools NOT Do?" id="what-cannot-do">
        <Callout type="warning" title="Tools Are Aids, Not Strategies">
          <p>
            No calculator tells you which bets to make. Tools handle arithmetic—they don't identify value, predict outcomes, or replace the analysis required for profitable betting.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identify good bets:</strong> Tools calculate; they don't analyze matchups or markets</li>
          <li><strong>Guarantee profits:</strong> Accurate calculations don't make unprofitable strategies profitable</li>
          <li><strong>Replace discipline:</strong> Knowing the right bet size doesn't help if you don't follow it</li>
          <li><strong>Predict outcomes:</strong> Probability math describes likelihood, not what will happen</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Available Tools" id="tools">
        <div class="tools-grid">
          {tools.map((tool) => (
            <LinkCard
              title={tool.title}
              href={tool.href}
              description={tool.description}
            />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="How to Use Tools Effectively" id="effective-use">
        <h3>Use them before betting, not after</h3>
        <p>
          Calculate potential outcomes and appropriate bet sizes before placing wagers. Post-hoc calculations don't help—they just show what you should have done.
        </p>

        <h3>Understand the underlying concepts</h3>
        <p>
          A parlay calculator is more useful if you understand why parlays are high-margin bets. An odds converter helps more if you understand implied probability. Tools should reinforce knowledge, not replace it.
        </p>

        <h3>Don't let tools encourage bad behavior</h3>
        <p>
          Seeing a big potential parlay payout can be exciting—that doesn't make the parlay a good bet. Use tools to evaluate, not to fantasize.
        </p>

        <h3>Combine with record-keeping</h3>
        <p>
          Track your bets honestly. Tools help with individual decisions; records help you see patterns over time.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <p>
          Tools are one component of a disciplined betting process. They help with:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Quick, accurate odds conversions across formats</li>
          <li>Understanding the true cost of parlays before placing them</li>
          <li>Calculating appropriate bet sizes to survive variance</li>
          <li>Removing mental math errors from your decision-making</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          But tools can't substitute for the hard work of analysis, bankroll discipline, and emotional control. They're useful additions to a sound process, not the process itself.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>Tools handle math; they don't identify value or predict outcomes</li>
          <li>Use calculators to support your process, not replace analysis</li>
          <li>Understand the concepts behind the calculations</li>
          <li>Don't let exciting potential payouts override disciplined decision-making</li>
          <li>Combine tools with record-keeping for maximum benefit</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content {
    padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0;
  }

  .quick-take {
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .quick-take h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .quick-take p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .tools-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .tools-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
